WEBVTT

00:00:04.770 --> 00:00:09.190
Labor: A robot specifically designed
for construction work.

00:00:09.860 --> 00:00:12.530
Labors allow dramatic advances
in construction...

00:00:12.530 --> 00:00:14.240
but also in crime.

00:00:14.570 --> 00:00:16.490
To combat these
new Labor crimes...

00:00:16.570 --> 00:00:19.910
the police created a special unit:
The Patrol Labor.

00:00:20.410 --> 00:00:23.080
And thus, the birth of Patlabor.

00:00:42.520 --> 00:00:49.110
moshimo ima anata no yume no eria ga
Should the area of your dreams

00:00:49.570 --> 00:00:53.780
namida ni okasare
Be invaded now by tears

00:00:55.740 --> 00:01:01.200
kujiketa toki wa nee kokoro de
When I faltered, in my heart

00:01:01.740 --> 00:01:07.750
watashi no namae yonde
My name calls

00:01:07.750 --> 00:01:12.000
hurry up hurry up ai no tsubasa
Hurry up, hurry up, the wings of love

00:01:13.090 --> 00:01:19.600
anata no sora e tonde yuku
Will fly to your sky

00:01:19.890 --> 00:01:23.850
I’m gonna fly fly away

00:01:23.850 --> 00:01:26.850
KONDISHON GUURIN
Condition green

00:01:26.850 --> 00:01:32.940
mukai kanashimi wo tasuketai no
Do you want to help this deep sorrow?

00:01:32.940 --> 00:01:35.950
Just fly fly away

00:01:35.950 --> 00:01:42.240
onaji itami wo mune no REDAA wa
The radar of your heart

00:01:42.370 --> 00:01:47.670
itsu demo kanjite iru wa
Is always feeling the same pain

00:01:49.880 --> 00:01:54.000
Just I'm gonna fly away

00:01:57.090 --> 00:02:01.100
Mass Market Product Plan

00:02:09.230 --> 00:02:11.020
Is it that late already?

00:02:20.530 --> 00:02:22.990
Another all-nighter
for the mechanics.

00:02:22.990 --> 00:02:26.750
It's probably like comparing a
normal car to a Formula 1.

00:02:26.750 --> 00:02:30.250
An Ingram takes a lot more work
than a simple production Labor.

00:02:30.830 --> 00:02:32.840
Well, I work on my skills a lot, too.

00:02:36.760 --> 00:02:37.340
If you don't mind...

00:02:37.340 --> 00:02:39.470
This is illegal.

00:02:39.470 --> 00:02:40.930
Don't be a spoilsport.

00:02:56.110 --> 00:02:59.450
So Asuma, if we used a
mass production model,

00:02:59.450 --> 00:03:02.570
would the mechanics have less work?

00:03:02.570 --> 00:03:04.280
Sure, compared to now.

00:03:04.280 --> 00:03:08.750
But we saw the economy
model at Haruumi. It was rejected.

00:03:10.460 --> 00:03:11.750
<i>That</i> model was rejected.

00:03:14.080 --> 00:03:18.670
But the next version is being
designed purely for police use.

00:03:20.630 --> 00:03:24.180
Division 1 is dying for an upgrade.

00:03:24.550 --> 00:03:27.430
But the important thing is,

00:03:30.060 --> 00:03:32.140
we do need a production
model for nationwide use.

00:03:41.490 --> 00:03:42.570
You don't believe me?

00:03:43.610 --> 00:03:46.120
If you say so, then it must be true.

00:03:46.120 --> 00:03:48.740
No, no, I mean about the
quality of the new version.

00:03:49.580 --> 00:03:52.120
I won't believe that
until I can test it.

00:03:54.920 --> 00:03:55.830
What?

00:03:55.830 --> 00:03:56.540
Nothing.

00:03:57.090 --> 00:03:58.210
You're weird.

00:04:01.590 --> 00:04:03.590
We've had some pretty rough months.

00:04:05.970 --> 00:04:08.060
What did you want to see me for?

00:04:09.350 --> 00:04:10.020
A business trip.

00:04:10.310 --> 00:04:10.810
Huh?

00:04:11.270 --> 00:04:17.610
Shinohara Industries has asked
us to test their new police Labor.

00:04:18.230 --> 00:04:19.440
It figures.

00:04:19.440 --> 00:04:20.070
What?

00:04:20.070 --> 00:04:21.990
Nothing.

00:04:22.780 --> 00:04:26.490
So I'm sending you
to their research lab.

00:04:26.490 --> 00:04:28.660
<i>I'm</i> doing the test?

00:04:29.120 --> 00:04:31.410
Yes, and Ota will
test it a few days later.

00:04:31.950 --> 00:04:34.160
I'm going to send Gomioka, too.

00:04:34.960 --> 00:04:38.420
But you get to be first.
Have fun.

00:04:38.880 --> 00:04:40.170
Yes, sir.

00:04:41.960 --> 00:04:43.010
Excuse me...

00:04:44.880 --> 00:04:45.840
Mr. Sakaki?

00:04:45.840 --> 00:04:46.970
I heard.

00:04:49.100 --> 00:04:51.890
Did you drop by just
to say goodbye to me?

00:04:52.730 --> 00:04:55.390
I'm not sure how I should test it.

00:04:55.980 --> 00:05:01.320
These tests are to find
problems in piloting and operation.

00:05:02.320 --> 00:05:08.240
Complain about anything
at all that doesn't feel right.

00:05:08.530 --> 00:05:14.710
Do your best. Your opinions will
help shape future police Labors.

00:05:15.460 --> 00:05:16.040
Yes, sir.

00:05:31.350 --> 00:05:34.680
...and that pushed it into
the heavyweight class.

00:05:35.640 --> 00:05:38.770
I think we've now got the
power up to a satisfactory level.

00:05:39.360 --> 00:05:44.110
We've completely redesigned
the data and control architecture.

00:05:44.110 --> 00:05:47.740
We've surpassed the Ingram
in total processing power.

00:05:47.910 --> 00:05:50.320
Of course... the architecture.

00:05:52.030 --> 00:05:57.120
Electronics have advanced
since the Ingram's day,

00:05:57.120 --> 00:06:00.420
so I'm afraid the poor
Ingram is showing its age.

00:06:23.480 --> 00:06:28.650
We built this facility entirely for
this test. It's top secret!

00:06:28.990 --> 00:06:29.780
Ready!

00:06:38.370 --> 00:06:40.960
It certainly looks impressive.

00:06:40.960 --> 00:06:42.750
You can't judge a book by its cover.

00:06:50.590 --> 00:06:55.060
The layout's the same, and
we're using the old monitor.

00:06:55.060 --> 00:06:55.970
Okay!

00:06:55.970 --> 00:07:00.020
Let's begin. Go slowly at first.

00:07:00.020 --> 00:07:02.520
Roger. Here I go.

00:07:02.520 --> 00:07:03.270
Go ahead.

00:07:37.220 --> 00:07:39.350
I don't feel much response.

00:07:57.120 --> 00:07:59.750
The handling is completely different.

00:08:09.920 --> 00:08:12.470
If it doesn't work easily,
don't strain yourself.

00:08:12.470 --> 00:08:13.970
Uh, okay!

00:08:15.300 --> 00:08:16.970
He doesn't move quite right.

00:08:26.310 --> 00:08:27.900
He's certainly strong.

00:08:34.200 --> 00:08:35.950
Well, it's not for me.

00:08:37.530 --> 00:08:43.370
So Gomioka gave it 80 points,
but you gave it only 60 points.

00:08:44.710 --> 00:08:46.670
You didn't have a
very good impression.

00:08:47.580 --> 00:08:50.210
He was way too sluggish.

00:08:50.670 --> 00:08:53.970
The controls didn't
have much feedback.

00:08:54.470 --> 00:08:56.220
He didn't respond well.

00:08:56.720 --> 00:09:00.430
It was pretty good
for a production model.

00:09:02.770 --> 00:09:05.940
The power issue
will be the big question.

00:09:07.060 --> 00:09:11.360
So Noa went two days ago,
and Gomioka went yesterday...

00:09:11.360 --> 00:09:15.320
The question is, what
will Ota think of today's test?

00:09:24.660 --> 00:09:26.710
How was it, Ota?

00:09:27.620 --> 00:09:29.460
Izumi, you're too biased.

00:09:31.090 --> 00:09:37.380
I know you love the
Ingrams, particularly Alphonse,

00:09:37.380 --> 00:09:42.100
but a test pilot has to be impartial!

00:09:44.270 --> 00:09:46.640
So what was your opinion?

00:09:46.640 --> 00:09:51.520
Come on, Izumi, why were
you so down on the new model?

00:09:53.190 --> 00:09:56.950
So, Ota, you gave the
new model a good score?

00:09:57.450 --> 00:10:01.950
Of course! Its strength alone
qualifies it to replace the Ingram.

00:10:02.370 --> 00:10:04.200
Don't you agree, Gomioka?

00:10:04.200 --> 00:10:09.670
I agree that it's strong,
but I've never used an Ingram.

00:10:12.540 --> 00:10:14.550
So you can't compare on that count.

00:10:18.380 --> 00:10:21.180
So we have a split vote in the jury.

00:10:35.980 --> 00:10:39.070
I think you'll be pleasantly surprised.

00:10:39.070 --> 00:10:40.200
Oh?

00:10:40.780 --> 00:10:42.450
Please begin.

00:10:42.450 --> 00:10:43.160
Yes.

00:10:50.830 --> 00:10:52.250
It's completely different.

00:10:56.340 --> 00:10:58.630
Is this even the same machine?

00:11:09.850 --> 00:11:10.810
Care for some coffee?

00:11:10.810 --> 00:11:12.600
No, thank you.

00:11:13.110 --> 00:11:14.020
Okay.

00:11:15.400 --> 00:11:17.190
It seemed different, didn't it?

00:11:17.190 --> 00:11:18.030
Sure did!

00:11:18.030 --> 00:11:20.030
It was like a different machine.

00:11:22.860 --> 00:11:27.490
It's still a bit sluggish, but the
jittery feeling is completely gone.

00:11:28.120 --> 00:11:31.620
That's all thanks to you,
Ota, and Gomioka.

00:11:31.620 --> 00:11:36.460
We're analyzing every
move you pilots make,

00:11:37.130 --> 00:11:40.550
then we recalibrate the
Labor's response to your inputs.

00:11:40.970 --> 00:11:48.470
We're optimizing for smoother,
more precise movement.

00:11:50.180 --> 00:11:52.390
So all our tests...

00:11:52.390 --> 00:11:59.360
You're helping gather data
through your piloting responses.

00:12:00.400 --> 00:12:05.820
The challenge was to
improve the economy model.

00:12:06.450 --> 00:12:08.660
This is our solution.

00:12:10.040 --> 00:12:16.380
We aim to create a production
model that's easy to operate.

00:12:18.500 --> 00:12:19.250
I think...

00:12:21.170 --> 00:12:23.260
I will have a cup
of coffee, after all.

00:12:24.300 --> 00:12:25.140
Heh, ok.

00:12:46.990 --> 00:12:50.410
A computer is just another tool.

00:12:52.120 --> 00:12:54.000
It can't do everything.

00:12:54.290 --> 00:12:59.250
Computer analysis is useful,
but take it with a grain of salt.

00:12:59.710 --> 00:13:00.630
But...

00:13:01.000 --> 00:13:05.340
Any machine with lots of moving
parts has its own idiosyncrasies.

00:13:11.220 --> 00:13:17.690
Even Labors of the same make
have differences between them.

00:13:18.440 --> 00:13:21.780
The servo power may differ.
The pilot has to compensate for that.

00:13:23.030 --> 00:13:24.740
I don't really understand.

00:13:27.110 --> 00:13:31.540
But couldn't that be compensated
for by computer control?

00:13:32.040 --> 00:13:33.290
It could.

00:13:33.870 --> 00:13:37.500
Then the skill of the
pilot is unimportant.

00:13:38.000 --> 00:13:43.960
If there are any problems with
the new model, complain to the techs.

00:13:44.550 --> 00:13:49.930
I don't know what to say.
I can't make up my mind.

00:13:50.430 --> 00:13:53.220
There's something not right about it.

00:14:06.280 --> 00:14:07.650
Take that!

00:14:12.950 --> 00:14:13.620
Well?

00:14:13.990 --> 00:14:16.660
Speed and power are
up 15%, on average.

00:14:21.630 --> 00:14:25.630
How long do you want to run
through these stupid exercises?

00:14:25.630 --> 00:14:28.340
For a real test, you
need a practice fight!

00:14:28.720 --> 00:14:31.050
I want a practice fight!

00:14:36.980 --> 00:14:38.230
It keeps getting better and better.

00:14:48.070 --> 00:14:49.610
She's fast!

00:14:49.610 --> 00:14:51.660
That's what a good
pilot can do for you.

00:14:52.120 --> 00:14:54.160
Did you capture that run?

00:14:54.160 --> 00:14:59.000
Of course. Mr. Gomioka should
match this time on his next run.

00:15:06.300 --> 00:15:08.630
It still doesn't feel quite right.

00:15:10.470 --> 00:15:12.930
...but you're still getting used to it.

00:15:13.260 --> 00:15:14.720
I guess so...

00:15:14.720 --> 00:15:19.600
I know it doesn't quite
have the feel of an Ingram.

00:15:20.190 --> 00:15:24.560
Yeah, but it seems like I
never quite hit what I'm aiming at.

00:15:26.150 --> 00:15:30.030
Our data shows that you're
only off by a few centimeters.

00:15:31.740 --> 00:15:34.620
That should certainly be good enough.

00:15:35.990 --> 00:15:39.200
We're very satisfied with these tests.

00:15:39.200 --> 00:15:42.040
This new model has turned
into a very impressive machine.

00:15:51.510 --> 00:15:53.590
What, a test fight?

00:15:53.590 --> 00:15:57.060
Yes. Upper management
has given the green light.

00:15:57.060 --> 00:16:03.440
And you want one of my men?
I see. Okay.

00:16:05.110 --> 00:16:07.860
They want a test
fight with an Ingram?

00:16:08.360 --> 00:16:10.110
They say the other tests are done.

00:16:11.030 --> 00:16:13.320
They sound pretty confident.

00:16:13.320 --> 00:16:16.830
They probably wouldn't ask for
a fight if they thought they'd lose.

00:16:18.540 --> 00:16:19.870
So who are you going to send?

00:16:20.580 --> 00:16:21.870
That's a problem...

00:16:23.040 --> 00:16:24.420
Captain!

00:16:25.040 --> 00:16:28.000
Why did you pick Izumi instead of me?

00:16:28.000 --> 00:16:31.170
You lost the coin toss.
Sorry.

00:16:31.170 --> 00:16:32.220
But...

00:16:32.220 --> 00:16:36.090
Are you accusing me of
cheating on the coin toss?

00:16:36.090 --> 00:16:37.970
No, sir, but...

00:16:38.560 --> 00:16:40.140
Next time, choose heads.

00:16:40.140 --> 00:16:43.440
But what if Izumi loses?
What then?

00:16:43.850 --> 00:16:45.190
Do you think that's likely?

00:16:45.190 --> 00:16:47.940
You don't know how
strong this new model is!

00:16:47.940 --> 00:16:49.900
I'm sure they'll show me.

00:16:50.480 --> 00:16:52.150
Captain!

00:16:53.530 --> 00:16:56.530
Please let me fight!

00:16:57.030 --> 00:16:58.910
Mind the shop while I'm gone.

00:17:03.500 --> 00:17:07.380
If he wants to do it so badly,
why can't we trade places?

00:17:07.710 --> 00:17:11.300
Captain, was that
coin toss on the level?

00:17:11.300 --> 00:17:15.300
You doubt me, too?
Does no one trust their captain?

00:17:15.930 --> 00:17:18.510
Are you afraid of
fighting this new model?

00:17:18.510 --> 00:17:23.100
Of course.
But that's not the problem.

00:17:24.140 --> 00:17:29.940
You think that if you lose,
we'll switch to the new model.

00:17:30.320 --> 00:17:31.440
Alphonse...

00:17:32.980 --> 00:17:34.280
won't lose.

00:17:46.370 --> 00:17:48.540
This is Yamamoto, one of our men.

00:17:48.540 --> 00:17:50.790
Pleased to meet you.

00:17:52.590 --> 00:17:55.010
Yamamoto just finished
his training here.

00:17:55.630 --> 00:18:00.350
He'll be using pre-programmed
reflexes taken from the tests.

00:18:00.850 --> 00:18:01.810
I see.

00:18:01.810 --> 00:18:04.770
The new model will attack.

00:18:04.770 --> 00:18:09.270
The Ingram must capture him.
Sound reasonable?

00:18:09.900 --> 00:18:11.820
Please try not to damage our Ingram.

00:18:12.360 --> 00:18:14.230
It'll be fine.

00:18:21.070 --> 00:18:22.200
Are you ready?

00:18:22.200 --> 00:18:22.660
Yes.

00:18:23.160 --> 00:18:24.700
Well, let's begin.

00:18:24.700 --> 00:18:27.120
Yes, thank you for your help.

00:18:45.680 --> 00:18:46.430
Ok, let's start.

00:19:04.620 --> 00:19:05.490
Impossible!

00:19:11.670 --> 00:19:12.960
It's not over yet!

00:19:23.800 --> 00:19:26.100
Yamamoto, that's enough.

00:19:42.160 --> 00:19:47.080
...so they've suspended plans
for a production model police Labor.

00:19:47.740 --> 00:19:50.960
There are no other upgrade
plans for Second Section.

00:19:53.250 --> 00:19:55.380
What do you think of that, Ota?

00:19:56.090 --> 00:19:58.340
What do you want me to say?

00:19:58.340 --> 00:19:59.380
Whatever.

00:20:00.050 --> 00:20:02.510
This must be hard on Division 1.

00:20:02.510 --> 00:20:05.850
Once again, their upgrade
plans have been derailed.

00:20:06.260 --> 00:20:08.810
They've canceled
the new police Labor,

00:20:08.810 --> 00:20:14.520
and Gomioka won't become
the captain of a new division.

00:20:14.520 --> 00:20:17.150
They said that?

00:20:17.570 --> 00:20:18.480
They will.

00:20:21.950 --> 00:20:27.580
I can't accept this!
Division 1 <i>needs</i> that new model,

00:20:27.580 --> 00:20:29.740
and we desperately
need new divisions!

00:20:30.120 --> 00:20:31.410
I understand your feelings.

00:20:31.790 --> 00:20:34.710
The new Labors may
have been production units,

00:20:34.710 --> 00:20:37.250
but they're vastly
superior to our Pythons!

00:20:37.250 --> 00:20:40.510
Think of what we could
do with those new machines!

00:20:43.800 --> 00:20:45.470
Lt. Gomioka...

00:20:46.930 --> 00:20:48.010
be patient.

00:20:50.220 --> 00:20:55.400
Could we do our job if Tokyo were
flooded with identical Labors?

00:20:56.150 --> 00:21:00.610
Anything that Division 1
receives must surpass the Ingram.

00:21:01.610 --> 00:21:03.610
That's what this
delay is really about.

00:21:04.650 --> 00:21:06.660
A Labor that surpasses the Ingram?

00:21:12.950 --> 00:21:18.580
I figured it out.
I know why the new model felt wrong.

00:21:20.000 --> 00:21:23.630
I complain and you adjust.

00:21:23.630 --> 00:21:28.760
You tweak and adjust
everything until it's perfect.

00:21:30.220 --> 00:21:35.980
We didn't go far enough. The new
model never got a custom tune-up.

00:21:38.310 --> 00:21:40.360
I just spoke with
Mr. Jitsuyama on the phone.

00:21:41.230 --> 00:21:45.570
He still has hopes for creating
a successor to the Ingram.

00:21:45.570 --> 00:21:46.490
Then...

00:21:46.900 --> 00:21:52.660
But he agrees, they can't match
our smooth, precise movements,

00:21:52.660 --> 00:21:59.130
without expert tuning
and top-notch piloting.

00:22:00.420 --> 00:22:03.630
And to get that in a
general-purpose Labor,

00:22:03.630 --> 00:22:07.380
it needs to adapt itself to
the idiosyncrasies of a single pilot.

00:22:08.380 --> 00:22:11.550
So it's back to the drawing board.

00:22:11.550 --> 00:22:16.480
He said he'll keep trying to
improve on the Ingram.

00:22:18.230 --> 00:22:20.610
We don't need a new model.

00:22:22.480 --> 00:22:24.570
Alphonse is perfect.

00:23:00.020 --> 00:23:04.020
arashi ga itsushika owatta
When I looked out, the storm had passed a long time ago.

00:23:06.110 --> 00:23:11.780
yuube no kobushi wa kirei ni
The morning dew betrays how yesterday's...

00:23:11.700 --> 00:23:13.740
arawareta
sorrows have been washed away.

00:23:14.990 --> 00:23:19.210
yoake ga NEJI wo yurumereba
Dawn is let loose by unbolting the panels of night.

00:23:21.080 --> 00:23:27.510
MASHIN ya BIRU ga mezameru
Even machines and the buildings all wake up.

00:23:28.300 --> 00:23:29.760
I got it

00:23:29.970 --> 00:23:37.310
tooku ga mieru yo PANORAMA mitai sa
Now I can see so far ahead, an unfolding panorama.

00:23:37.470 --> 00:23:43.190
doko kara mite mo heiwa-na Happy Island
Wherever I watch from, I see a peaceful, happy island.

00:23:43.310 --> 00:23:44.730
One more chance

00:23:44.940 --> 00:23:52.360
kimi ni oshietai kimi ni tsutaetai
The thing I want to tell to you, the thing I want to show to you

00:23:52.490 --> 00:23:57.830
yume no GEITO ga me no mae de
The shining gate to our dreams lays open to us...

00:23:58.540 --> 00:24:01.500
ima hiraku yo
right now before our eyes.

00:24:07.000 --> 00:24:11.010
This story is fiction...

00:24:07.000 --> 00:24:11.010
but in 10 years, who knows?

00:24:16.800 --> 00:24:19.930
A scary monster awakens near
a small town off the coast.

00:24:19.930 --> 00:24:23.810
One of the town's elders tells us
a mysterious legend.

00:24:23.810 --> 00:24:26.560
Let's meet up with that monster.
Do you see him?

00:24:26.560 --> 00:24:28.070
How will we make him come out?

00:24:28.070 --> 00:24:34.700
Science versus myth.
Isn't it romantic?

00:24:34.990 --> 00:24:38.870
Next episode: Orders of the Coast Guard
Target, locked on!

00:24:37.830 --> 00:24:43.120
Next episode

00:24:37.830 --> 00:24:43.120
Orders of the Coast Guard
